      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 4-year-old boy had infantile bronchial asthma resistant to treatment. He was referred for a febrile respiratory distress which led to the diagnosis of periesophagus mediastinis mass with erosion of both contiguous vertebral discs. The oesophagogram showed a foreign body in an esophageal diverticulum. After its extraction, all pulmonary symptoms disappeared."},
